   "url": "https://x.com/TruthAgape/status/2102446056529170756",
   "conversationId": "2102446056529170756",
   "text": "I am team:\n\nNeither accountability nor grace/mercy can be all or nothing.\n\nAccountability is necessary (but not necessarily sufficient) for restoration and reconciliation. It is not dependent upon forgivenss. You can take accountability and never be forgiven by the person you hurt.\n\nForgiveness can be done without any accountability, but does not require nor force restoration or reconciliation. It is a personal experience regarding something or someone that happened to you. You are not required to share it with anyone. Nor are you required to remove boundaries that keep you safe if the offender did not take accountability.\n\nI am so fatigued by this idea that to hold people accountable, in general, we must do away with grace or mercy. I am also so fatigued with the idea that offering grace and mercy means we have to do away with accountability.\n\nGrace and mercy work quite nicely alongside accountability. I would argue they work best when accountability is willingly pursued and should be applied sparingly and strategically when accountability is avoided.",
   "lang": "en",
   "createdAt": "2026-09-22T17:12:56.000Z",
   "type": "tweet",
