   "id": "2097482955379683440",
   "url": "https://x.com/TruthAgape/status/2097482955379683440",
   "conversationId": "2097482955379683440",
   "text": "As a part of my work, I have volunteered to mentor women in jail or prison. I had the opportunity to mentor a young woman who was facing a charge of death of a minor due to neglect, a.k.a negligent homicide. \n\nIn many ways, she and I aren't so different. Perhaps, I am more culpable than she. We were both addicted to drugs and in absuive relationships. Her boyfriend killed her son. I aborted mine. Everytime I looked into her eyes, I saw myself a decade earlier, scared and hopeless.\n\nYet, she faced decades in prison and people continue to try to tell me how empowered I am. \n\nI will never stop being deeply aware of how much I need Jesus and how blessed I am to have the honor to serve others during the hardest moments of their lives, even if they are self-inflicted.",
   "lang": "en",
   "createdAt": "2026-09-09T00:31:20.000Z",
   "type": "tweet",
   "author": {
